# Part 17 — mobile material: glass navigation and no decorative outlines

Date: 01.09.2026. Scope: pages 22–23 only; pages 16–20 are protected.

Owner decisions:

- use glassmorphism for `shared/MobileBottomNav`;
- remove decorative closed outlines from passive mobile cards, current-lesson blocks, lesson rows and the outer nav plane;
- preserve functional borders: focus-visible, form controls, errors, secondary buttons, dropzones, separators and status rings;
- depth comes from surface, spacing and existing neutral elevation; the accepted current-lesson illumination remains the only colored glow;
- no additional colored-shadow token;
- auth glass is not reused;
- new variables are allowed only as the already approved mobile glass package.

Approved package:

- `component/mobile-bottom-nav/glass-surface-opacity`: dark 78%, light 90%, `FLOAT`, scope `OPACITY`;
- `component/mobile-bottom-nav/glass-background-blur`: dark/light 20 px, `FLOAT`, scope `EFFECT_FLOAT`;
- `material/glass/chrome/base`: background blur bound to the blur variable plus the existing `shadow/raised` geometry and color binding; no stroke.

Implementation gate:

- add one absolute `glass-surface` rectangle behind the item instances in each of the three nav variants;
- bind only that rectangle's opacity, never the component root;
- keep the content at opacity 1;
- remove fills, strokes and effects from each nav component root;
- remove decorative strokes from the agreed 20 current mobile fixture nodes;
- write sequentially and read back after every frame or bounded mutation group;
- do not publish.

Stop after this material party and show the owner before the student probe.
